BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Gunfight at the O.K. Corral in VistaVision
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260821T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260821T223000
DTSTAMP:20260808T084056Z
UID:019de50d-75de-011b-6835-d2abcb4adec8@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:In person: actor Peter Weller\n\nFriday\, August 21\, 2026 at 
 7:30 pm\n\nLocation: Academy Museum of Motion Pictures\n\nRuntime: 2h 2m\n
 \n1957 | 122 min. | USA | Color | English | VistaVision \nDIRECTED BY: Joh
 n Sturges \nWRITTEN BY: Leon Uris \nWITH: Burt Lancaster\, Kirk Douglas\, 
 Rhonda Fleming\, Jo Van Fleet\n\nType: Screenings\n\nJohn Sturges (The Mag
 nificent Seven\, 1960) directed this vivid re-telling of the classic Weste
 rn set in 1880s Arizona. Burt Lancaster is Marshal Wyatt Earp\, who partne
 rs with his brothers to clean up the town of Tombstone. Helped by loyal fr
 iend Doc Holliday (Kirk Douglas)\, they find themselves embroiled in a dea
 dly conflict with the Clanton family. The second film to team Lancaster an
 d Douglas\, Gunfight was nominated for its film editing and sound recordin
 g and features a rousing score by four-time Oscar winner Dimitri Tiomkin (
 High Noon\, 1952)\, with a memorable title song performed by Frankie Laine
 . In 1967\, Sturges continued the story with Hour of the Gun\, starring Ja
 mes Garner as Earp and Jason Robards as Holliday.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/gunfight-at-the-o-k-c
 orral-in-vista-vision-019de50d-75de-011b-6835-d2abcb4adec8
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Nancy Drew
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260822T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260822T121500
DTSTAMP:20260808T084056Z
UID:019db103-fddd-6a12-cf78-c41fe1e4486c@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:Saturday\, August 22\, 2026 at 11 am\n\nLocation: Academy Muse
 um of Motion Pictures\n\nRuntime: 1h 37m\n\n2007 | 97 min. | USA | Color |
  Scope | English | Rated PG | DCP \nDIRECTED BY: Andrew Fleming \nWRITTEN
  BY: Andrew Fleming\, Tiffany Paulsen \nSTORY BY: Tiffany Paulsen \nWITH: 
 Emma Roberts\, Josh Flitter\, Max Thieriot\, Tate Donovan\n\nType: Screeni
 ngs\n\nEmma Roberts steps into the role of Nancy Drew in this contemporary
  adaptation of the iconic teen detective. When Nancy’s father (Tate Dono
 van) gets a job that moves them to Los Angeles\, he encourages her to beha
 ve like an average teenager and refrain from sleuthing. Unable to refrain 
 from her passion\, Nancy dives into a famous cold case involving the death
  of a movie star. The subject of hundreds of novels\, and numerous film\, 
 television and video game adaptations\, the character of Nancy Drew has be
 en inspiring young women since the 1930s.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/nancy-drew-019db103-f
 ddd-6a12-cf78-c41fe1e4486c
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Ten Commandments in VistaVision
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260822T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260822T133000
DTSTAMP:20260808T084056Z
UID:019de50f-21df-5b2b-aa64-3ac6e6d9ce9e@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:In person: Charlotte Barker\, senior director\, film preservat
 ion and restoration\, Paramount Archives\; and Craig Barron\, executive d
 irector\, Magnopus\n\nSaturday\, August 22\, 2026 at 12 pm\n\nLocation: Ac
 ademy Museum of Motion Pictures\n\nRuntime: 3h 39m\n\n1956 | 219 min | USA
  | Color | English | Rated G | VistaVision \nDIRECTED BY: Cecil B. DeMill
 e \nWRITTEN BY: Aeneas MacKenzie\, Jesse Lasky Jr.\, Jack Gariss\, Fredri
 c M. Frank \nWITH: Charlton Heston\, Yul Brynner\, Anne Baxter\, Edward G
 . Robinson\n\nType: Screenings\n\nThe final film directed by blockbuster m
 aster Cecil B. DeMille is a lavish remake of his own 1923 silent epic. Cha
 rlton Heston\, as Moses\, leads a stellar cast\, including Yul Brynner as 
 Pharaoh Rameses II\, Anne Baxter as the lustful Nefretiri\, and Edward G. 
 Robinson as the rebellious Dathan. The film was nominated for seven Oscars
 \, including Best Picture\, and John Fulton (The Invisible Man\, 1933) won
  for its special effects\, which included such classic Biblical sequences 
 as the Burning bush\, the Ten Plagues\, and the parting of the Red Sea.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/the-ten-commandments-
 in-vista-vision-019de50f-21df-5b2b-aa64-3ac6e6d9ce9e
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:An Evening with Charlize Theron Featuring Mad Max: Fury Road
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260822T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260822T213000
DTSTAMP:20260808T084056Z
UID:019f24e4-20c3-8b06-55f7-05f9a1187e85@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Conversations,Screenings
DESCRIPTION:Charlize Theron engages in conversation with members of the Ac
 ademy Museum Teen Council before a special screening of Mad Max: Fury Road
  (2015).\n\nSaturday\, August 22\, 2026 at 7 pm\n\nLocation: Academy Museu
 m of Motion Pictures\n\nRuntime: 2h\n\nSchedule\n7pm | Conversation \n7:4
 0pm | Screening\n2015 | 120 min. | Australia | Color | Scope | English | D
 CP \nDIRECTOR: George Miller\nWRITTEN BY: George Miller\, Brendan McCarthy
 \, Nico Lathouris\nWITH: Tom Hardy\, Charlize Theron\, Nicholas Hoult\, Hu
 gh Keays-Byrne\n\nType: Conversations\, Screenings\n\nGeorge Miller return
 ed to the memorable post-apocalyptic world he created for Mad Max with thi
 s nonstop thrill ride that introduced a new Max (Tom Hardy) as well as a m
 emorable action heroine (Charlize Theron as Imperator Furiosa). The film r
 eceived 10 nominations including Best Picture and Directing\, and earned O
 scars for Costume Design\, Film Editing\, Makeup and Hairstyling\, Product
 ion Design\, Sound Editing\, and Sound Mixing.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/an-evening-with-charl
 ize-theron-featuring-mad-max-fury-road-019f24e4-20c3-8b06-55f7-05f9a1187e8
 5
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Funny Face
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260823T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260823T133000
DTSTAMP:20260808T084056Z
UID:019dff3e-49fd-4d34-726a-fa34142e7d20@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:Sunday\, August 23\, 2026 at 11 am\n\nLocation: Academy Museum
  of Motion Pictures\n\nRuntime: 1h 43m\n\n1957 | 103 min. | USA | Technico
 lor | English | Not Rated | DCP  \nDIRECTED BY: Stanley Donen  \nWRITTEN
  BY: Leonard Gershe \nWITH: Audrey Hepburn\, Fred Astaire\, Kay Thompson\
 , Michael Auclair\n\nType: Screenings\n\nStanley Donen directed this charm
 ing May-December romantic musical comedy that pokes fun at the world of fa
 shion photography and features songs by George and Ira Gershwin\, as well 
 as Technicolor cinematography of Paris locations. Fred Astaire plays the p
 hotographer (inspired by Richard Avedon\, whose work appears in the film)\
 , and Audrey Hepburn is the shy bookshop assistant who becomes his model a
 nd muse.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/funny-face-019dff3e-4
 9fd-4d34-726a-fa34142e7d20
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Jackie
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260823T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260823T160000
DTSTAMP:20260808T084056Z
UID:019d8803-b2c0-a887-a0ba-9fdddd5907b3@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:Sunday\, August 23\, 2026 at 2 pm\n\nLocation: Academy Museum 
 of Motion Pictures\n\nRuntime: 1h 40m\n\n2016 | 100 min. | USA/France/Chil
 e | Color | English | Rated R | DCP \nDIRECTED BY: Pablo Larraín \nWRITTE
 N BY: Noah Oppenheim \nWITH: Natalie Portman\, Peter Sarsgaard\, Greta Ger
 wig\, Billy Crudup\n\nType: Screenings\n\nNatalie Portman was nominated fo
 r her uncanny performance as Jacqueline Bouvier Kennedy in this unusual bi
 opic directed by Pablo Larraín (Maria\, 2024). The screenplay by Noah Opp
 enheim is structured around an interview by a magazine journalist (Billy C
 rudup) and focuses on key events in the First Lady’s life\, especially t
 he assassination of her husband. The film was also nominated for Madeline 
 Fontaine’s authentic costume designs and the unsettling score by Mica Le
 vi (Under the Skin\, 2013)\, which used flutes and strings to evoke its he
 roine’s combination of vulnerability and resilience.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/jackie-019d8803-b2c0-
 a887-a0ba-9fdddd5907b3
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Hot Spell
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260823T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260823T170000
DTSTAMP:20260808T084056Z
UID:019de511-03b4-d950-feef-fa89b7d15a45@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:Sunday\, August 23\, 2026 at 3 pm\n\nLocation: Academy Museum 
 of Motion Pictures\n\nRuntime: 1h 26m\n\n1958 | 86 min. | USA | Black-and-
 White | English | Not Rated | DCP \nDIRECTED BY: Daniel Mann \nWRITTEN B
 Y: James Poe \nWITH: Shirley Booth\, Anthony Quinn\, Shirley MacLaine\, E
 arl Holliman\n\nType: Screenings\n\nBased on the unproduced play Next of K
 in\, Hot Spell is a New Orleans-set drama about matriarch Alma\, whose bou
 ndless optimism stands at odds with her husband John’s philandering and 
 her adult children’s desire to move on from the family home. Set during 
 one sweltering summer evening\, screenwriter James Poe\, who also adapted 
 Tennessee Williams’s Cat on a Hot Tin Roof (1958)\, slowly ratchets up t
 he pressure on the tenuous facade of the happy mid-century nuclear family.
  Starring a trifecta of Oscar winners—Shirley Booth (Come Back\, Little 
 Sheba\, 1952)\, Anthony Quinn (Wild is the Wind\, 1958\; Zorba the Greek\,
  1964)\, Shirley MacLaine (Terms of Endearment\, 1983)—and supported by 
 another—Eileen Heckart (Butterflies Are Free\, 1972) as Alma’s jaded b
 est friend—this tender\, layered production offers a heartbreaking view 
 of generational tensions and the nuances of family dynamics.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/hot-spell-019de511-03
 b4-d950-feef-fa89b7d15a45
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:White Christmas in VistaVision
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260823T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260823T223000
DTSTAMP:20260808T084056Z
UID:019de512-76dc-82b2-35eb-c7b2f9f6791e@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:Sunday\, August 23\, 2026 at 7:30 pm\n\nLocation: Academy Muse
 um of Motion Pictures\n\nRuntime: 2h\n\n1954 | 120 min. | USA | Color | En
 glish | VistaVision \nDIRECTED BY: Michael Curtiz \nWRITTEN BY: Norman Kra
 sna\, Norman Panama\, Melvin Frank \nWITH: Bing Crosby\, Danny Kaye\, Rose
 mary Clooney\, Vera-Ellen\n\nType: Screenings\n\nThis popular musical come
 dy inspired by Irving Berlin’s Oscar-winning song from Holiday Inn (1942
 ) was the first feature to be filmed and released in VistaVision. Bing Cro
 sby and Danny Kaye star as war veterans and entertainers who become romant
 ically involved with a sister act (Rosemary Clooney and Vera-Ellen). Direc
 ted by Oscar winner Michael Curtiz (Casablanca\, 1943)\, White Christmas f
 eatures delightful musical numbers spotlighting more than a dozen Irving B
 erlin songs\, including the nominated “Count Your Blessings (Instead of 
 Sheep)”.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/white-christmas-in-vi
 sta-vision-019de512-76dc-82b2-35eb-c7b2f9f6791e
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Secret World of Arrietty
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260824T143000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260824T150000
DTSTAMP:20260808T084056Z
UID:019dd521-7b44-c524-f75d-3935ed4b9d41@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:Monday\, August 24\, 2026 at 2:30 pm\n\nLocation: Academy Muse
 um of Motion Pictures\n\nRuntime: 1h 34m\n\n2010 | 94 min. | Japan | Color
  | Japanese with English subtitles| Rated G | DCP \nDIRECTED BY: Hiromasa 
 Yonebayashi \nWRITTEN BY: Hayao Miyazaki\, Keiko Niwa \nWITH: Mirai Shid
 a\, Ryunosuke Kamiki\, Tatsuya Fujiwara\, Tomokazu Miura\n\nType: Screenin
 gs\n\nDebut director Hiromasa Yonebayashi (When Marnie Was There\, 2014) a
 nd Studio Ghibli teamed up for this film version of Mary Norton’s 1952 c
 hildren’s classic The Borrowers\, full of gorgeous imagery of the natura
 l world. Arrietty is the daughter of a family of Borrowers—miniature peo
 ple secretly living in an occupied house—who risk their home when she be
 friends a human boy.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/the-secret-world-of-a
 rrietty-019dd521-7b44-c524-f75d-3935ed4b9d41
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Anything Goes in VistaVision
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260824T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260824T223000
DTSTAMP:20260808T084056Z
UID:019de513-00e0-5754-7620-1708e4e8d8c2@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:Monday\, August 24\, 2026 at 7:30 pm\n\nLocation: Academy Muse
 um of Motion Pictures\n\nRuntime: 1h 46m\n\n1956 | 106 min. | USA | Techni
 color | English | Not Rated | VistaVision  \nDIRECTED BY: Robert Lewis  
 \nWRITTEN BY: Sidney Sheldon  \nWITH: Bing Crosby\, Donald O’Connor\, J
 eanmaire\, Mitzi Gaynor\n\nType: Screenings\n\nSeasoned performer Bill Ben
 son (Bing Crosby) and rising star Ted Adams (Donald O’Connor) team up to
  find the perfect leading lady for their new Broadway show. Each performer
  finds a compelling talent—American Patsy Blair (Mitzi Gaynor) and Frenc
 h nightclub star Gaby Duval (Jeanmaire)—and the conflict of who to cast 
 heightens the stakes. Blending backstage drama with a bit of farce\, this 
 beloved narrative offers a musical spectacle driven as much by personal ri
 sk as ambition. The film represents a significant first: Robert Lewis’s 
 solo directorial debut after a storied career with The Group Theater. It a
 lso marks a historic last as Crosby’s final film for Paramount Pictures 
 during the waning years of his film career.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/anything-goes-in-vist
 a-vision-019de513-00e0-5754-7620-1708e4e8d8c2
END:VEVENT
