UID:019f1fdb-7bb1-0d3a-96fc-ec6cc22ce4f2@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:Calling all creatures of the night: join the Academy Museum fo
 r a fang-tastic day exploring the vampire\, the most famous creature of th
 e dark\, with special-effects demos\, thrilling tours\, monster appearance
 s\, and more.\n\nSaturday\, October 24\, 2026 at 11 am\n\nLocation: Academ
 y Museum of Motion Pictures\n\nRuntime: 1h 30m\n\nAt a glance\n11am | Movi
 e | Hotel Transylvania (2012) | Ted Mann Theater\n11am–1:30pm | Special 
 effects makeup and hair demo | Grand Lobby  \n1–5pm | Monster meet and g
 reet | Grand Lobby  \n1:30\, 2:30\, and 3:30pm | The Horror Tours | Level 
 4\n2:30pm | Movie | Blade (1998) | Ted Mann Theater \n4–5pm | Killer Fit
 ness performance and dance-along | Grand Lobby    \n7:30pm | Movie | Horro
 r of Dracula (1958) | Ted Mann Theater \nMonster Mash offers early access 
 for Academy Museum members. Please check back for ticket sale information.
 \n\nType: Screenings\n\nCalling all creatures of the night: join the Acade
 my Museum for a fang-tastic day of special-effects makeup demonstrations\,
  thrilling tours\, monster appearances\, movies\, and activities—all exp
 loring the vampire\, the famous creature of the dark. Embrace this year’
 s theme with Dracula\, vampire hunters\, and a relaxing monster resort.  \
 nFree with the purchase of a general admission ticket. Museum admission is
  free for youth 17 and under. \nDetails\n11am | Movie | Hotel Transylvania
  (2012) | Ted Mann Theater | Lower Level 2\nRated PG\n11am–1:30pm | Spec
 ial effects makeup and hair demo | Grand Lobby  \nA scary-good time with t
 ransformations by special effects makeup artist Gabi Gonzalez\, hair styli
 st Johnny Villanueva\, and Academy Award winner Howard Berger.\nGeneral ad
 mission ticket not required. Program may end early.  \n11am–1:30pm | Vam
 pire blood special effects family workshop | Shirley Temple Education Stud
 io | Lower Level 1\nGet mixed up in the world of horror makeup with a less
 on on creating Hollywood-worthy vampire blood\, featuring tools used by re
 al artists. All ages are welcome.\n1–5pm | Monster meet and greet | Gran
 d Lobby  \nMeet Universal Studios' classic movie monsters—Dracula\, the 
 Bride of Frankenstein\, and Frankenstein's monster—for a can't-miss phot
 o opportunity. It’ll be a scream.  \nGeneral admission ticket not requir
 ed. Monsters meet for 30 minutes at a time.   \n1:30\, 2:30\, and 3:30pm |
  The Horror Tours | Level 4\nOpen the door and peek inside—if you dare
 —with a museum educator on a 30-minute guide tour of The Horror Show exh
 ibition. Get a behind-the-scenes look at the representation of vampires an
 d gothic horror in film\, and explore the production processes for many ho
 rror classics.\nTours are limited to 25 people and are first-come\, first-
 served. Please arrive at the meeting place on Level 4 up to 10 minutes bef
 ore the start time to secure your spot. General admission ticket required.
    \n2:30pm | Movie | Blade (1998) | Ted Mann Theater | Lower Level 2\nRat
 ed R \n4–5pm | Killer Fitness performance and dance-along | Grand Lobby 
    \nA horror performance and dance-along\, where fitness meets fear. \n7:
 30pm | Movie | Horror of Dracula (1958) | Ted Mann Theater | Lower Level 2
 \nNot Rated \nMonster Mash offers early access for Academy Museum members.
  Please check back for ticket sale information.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/monster-mash-019f1fdb
 -7bb1-0d3a-96fc-ec6cc22ce4f2
END:VEVENT
